# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "OCaml client binding for rayforce's embeddable C API"
description: """
Thin FFI binding over rayforce.h's client-side surface: runtime init, IPC connect/send/send_async, and the atom/vector/table/list/dict constructors needed to build values to ship over IPC. Also covers the embedded-runtime surface (ray_eval_str, env get/set, poll run/exit) for hosting rayforce's interpreter directly inside the calling process instead of talking to a separate server.

Needs a librayforce.a/.so to link against. The ~/code/aur/rayforce package (pkgrel 2+) installs it plus a pkg-config file, which this library's dune rule picks up automatically. On a machine without that package, point RAYFORCE_LIBDIR/RAYFORCE_INCDIR at a `rayforce` checkout built with `make` (produces librayforce.a at the repo root) instead."""
maintainer: ["Vincent Bernardoff <vb@luminar.eu.org>"]
authors: ["Vincent Bernardoff <vb@luminar.eu.org>"]
license: "ISC"
depends: [
  "dune" {>= "3.24"}
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14.0"}
  "dune-configurator"
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
x-maintenance-intent: ["(latest)"]
